ntdll: a RAM cap is a ceiling on free memory, not a debt against it.

WINE_RAM_REPORTING_BIAS subtracted the whole bias from available memory as
well as from the total. A 15.2 GB phone capped to 6 GB has a 9 GB bias and
5 to 8.5 GB really free, so get_performance_info reported 0 bytes free, every
time. Empyrion's startup check wants 8 GB free: "Low memory detected" on every
launch, and its textures dropped to the lowest setting.

Free memory is now the real MemAvailable, clamped to the capped total. Swap is
no longer charged the shortfall.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
@@ -2849,13 +2849,23 @@
             fclose(fp);
             totalram -= min( totalram, ram_reporting_bias );
             if (mem_available) freeram = mem_available;
-            if ((long long)freeram >= ram_reporting_bias) freeram -= ram_reporting_bias;
-            else
-            {
-                long long bias = ram_reporting_bias - freeram;
-                freeswap -= min( bias, freeswap );
-                freeram = 0;
-            }
+            /* Vessel: a RAM cap is a ceiling on what is free, not a debt
+             * against it.
+             *
+             * This used to subtract the whole bias from available memory as
+             * well as from the total, and take any shortfall out of swap. On
+             * a 15.2 GB phone capped to 6 GB the bias is 9 GB, so with the 5
+             * to 8.5 GB a phone actually has free, every program was told it
+             * had none: Empyrion's startup check wants 8 GB free, printed
+             * "Low memory detected" on every launch and dropped its textures
+             * to the lowest setting, and would have at any cap below the
+             * device's size.
+             *
+             * What a cap means is that no more than the capped total can be
+             * available, so that is what is reported: the real figure, never
+             * above the total the program was given. Swap is left alone -- the
+             * bias was never swap's to pay. */
+            if (ram_reporting_bias && freeram > totalram) freeram = totalram;
         }
     }
 #elif defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__FreeBSD_kernel__) || defined(__NetBSD__) || \
